&lt;p&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;  CIM 50-20, CIM 50-20.1&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  A diagnostic pap smear and related medically necessary services are covered under Medicare Part B when ordered by a physician under one of the following conditions:&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;  
&lt;li&gt;  Previous cancer of the cervix, uterus, or vagina that has been or is presently being treated;&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;  Previous abnormal pap smear;&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;  Any abnormal findings of the vagina, cervix, uterus, ovaries, or adnexa;&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;  Any significant complaint by the patient referable to the female reproductive system; or&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;  Any signs or symptoms that might in the physician&#39;s judgment reasonably be related to a gynecologic disorder.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  Screening Pap Smears and Pelvic Examinations for Early Detection of Cervical or Vaginal Cancer.  (See section &lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;details&sol;ncd-details.aspx?NCDId=185&amp;ncdver=3&quot;&gt;210.2&lt;&sol;a&gt;.)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
